{"name":"Topiary Garden","hex":"#6f7c00","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"topiary","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of, or relating to art of topiaries.","Of a tree or shrub, trimmed in artistic shape."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Art or practice of trimming shrubs or trees in artistic or ornamental shapes, e.g. of animals.","A garden decorated with such art."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/topiary"},{"term":"garden","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An outdoor area containing one or more types of plants, usually plants grown for food or ornamental purposes.","Such an ornamental place to which the public have access."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To grow plants in a garden; to create or maintain a garden.","Of a batsman, to inspect and tap the pitch lightly with the bat so as to smooth out small rough patches and irregularities."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/garden"}],"entries":[{"title":"Topiary Park","blocks":[{"text":"Topiary Park is a 9.2-acre (3.7 ha) public park and garden in Columbus, Ohio's Discovery District. The park's topiary garden, officially the Topiary Garden at Old Deaf School Park, is designed to depict figures from Georges Seurat's 1884 painting, A Sunday Afternoon on the Island of La Grande Jatte. It is the only park based entirely on a painting."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/59/Topiary_Park%2C_Columbus%2C_OH.jpg/330px-Topiary_Park%2C_Columbus%2C_OH.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Topiary_Park","wikidata":"Q57515888"},{"title":"Topiary","blocks":[{"text":"Topiary is the horticultural practice of training perennial plants by clipping the foliage and twigs of trees, shrubs and subshrubs to develop and maintain clearly defined shapes, whether geometric or fanciful. The term also refers to plants which have been shaped in this way. As an art form it is a type of living sculpture. The word derives from the Latin word for an ornamental landscape gardener, topiarius, a creator of topia or \"places\", a Greek word that Romans also applied to fictive indoor landscapes executed in fresco."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ec/Cementerio%2C_Tulc%C3%A1n%2C_Ecuador%2C_2015-07-21%2C_DD_60.JPG/330px-Cementerio%2C_Tulc%C3%A1n%2C_Ecuador%2C_2015-07-21%2C_DD_60.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Topiary","wikidata":"Q1437791"},{"title":"Garden","blocks":[{"text":"A garden is a planned space, usually outdoors, set aside for the cultivation, display, and enjoyment of plants and other forms of nature. The single feature identifying even the wildest wild garden is control. The garden can incorporate both natural and artificial materials."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/41/Brooklyn_Botanic_Garden_New_York_May_2015_010.jpg/330px-Brooklyn_Botanic_Garden_New_York_May_2015_010.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Garden","wikidata":"Q1107656"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f2/Columbus%2C_Ohio_JJ_60-crop.jpg/500px-Columbus%2C_Ohio_JJ_60-crop.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f2/Columbus%2C_Ohio_JJ_60-crop.jpg/1280px-Columbus%2C_Ohio_JJ_60-crop.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f2/Columbus%2C_Ohio_JJ_60-crop.jpg/500px-Columbus%2C_Ohio_JJ_60-crop.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Aerial view in autumn","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AColumbus%2C_Ohio_JJ_60-crop.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9a/CML_Main_Library_new_wing.jpg/500px-CML_Main_Library_new_wing.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9a/CML_Main_Library_new_wing.jpg/1280px-CML_Main_Library_new_wing.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9a/CML_Main_Library_new_wing.jpg/500px-CML_Main_Library_new_wing.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Parkland and seating adjoining the Columbus Metropolitan Library to the park","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACML_Main_Library_new_wing.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fd/Topiary_Park%2C_Columbus%2C_OH_01.jpg/500px-Topiary_Park%2C_Columbus%2C_OH_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fd/Topiary_Park%2C_Columbus%2C_OH_01.jpg/1280px-Topiary_Park%2C_Columbus%2C_OH_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fd/Topiary_Park%2C_Columbus%2C_OH_01.jpg/500px-Topiary_Park%2C_Columbus%2C_OH_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A section of the park","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATopiary_Park%2C_Columbus%2C_OH_01.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8a/Columbus%2C_Ohio_aerial_view_of_Deaf_School_Park-crop.jpg/330px-Columbus%2C_Ohio_aerial_view_of_Deaf_School_Park-crop.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8a/Columbus%2C_Ohio_aerial_view_of_Deaf_School_Park-crop.jpg/960px-Columbus%2C_Ohio_aerial_view_of_Deaf_School_Park-crop.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thu